## 1. Speaking anxiety
Before speaking in front of audience, we often feel nervous, your heart races, the hand shakes, and your voice ... Sometimes, we do not understand why we become like this. 
For example, I made a 3-minute speech in the Toastmaster club several days ago. Before making the speech, I tried to tell my brain that "I come here to learn and practice my public speaking, do not worry". I felt calm down and enjoyed the others' speeches. 
However, when it came to my turn, my heart suddenly raced faster, my hand was shaking, and my words was wiggling. At that time, I did not know why because in my head, I did not worry but I could not control my body.
After that, I watched many videos about public speaking and read relevant books. 
I acknowledge that because we are humans, these behaviours are our inherent characteristics of humans. They happen natuarally. What we can do is to learn to reduce them.
One of powerful techniques I have learned is to control our breath. Learning how to take a deep breath: inhale, exhale slowly. The time for exhalation should be double that of inhalation.
It actually works for me. 
